        "original_id": "249fc998-9013-5236-be7d-da4332328362",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Murray Head, Tim Rice, Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Works: “One Night in Bangkok”, “Superstar”, Jesus Christ Superstar, Chess, Say It Ain't So\n- Roles: actor, singer\n\nFacts:\n- Murray Seafield St George Head was born on 5 March 1946 and is an English actor and singer.\n- Murray Head is most recognized for the international hit song “Superstar” from the 1970 rock opera Jesus Christ Superstar.\n- Murray Head released the album Say It Ain't So in 1975.\n- “One Night in Bangkok” is a song from the concept album and subsequent musical Chess.\n- Murray Head is most recognized for “One Night in Bangkok,” the 1984 single from Chess that topped the charts in various countries.\n- Chess was created by Tim Rice, Benny Andersson, and Björn Ulvaeus.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
